notes: The usual explanation is AI style — a font, a gradient, a layout. I don't think that's it. The deck I recognized was complete in a way a person rarely is. Every point had a slide; every slide had a heading; every heading had three bullets. Completeness was the problem. A person makes a deck by deciding what not to say. A short post I read described this as covering everything, and it named what I had been feeling. The fix had to be upstream of layout.
